From 5f480edeccf643a36db925e23217891e387ab412 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mesa-nvk-horizon <mesa-nvk-horizon@localhost>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 22:19:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/30] meson: do not require libdl where there is no dynamic
 loader
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

meson.build hard-failed with "C shared or static library 'dl' not found"
whenever dlopen was absent from the C library. That treats libdl as the
only reason dlopen could be missing, which is true of older glibc but
not of a C library that has no dynamic loader at all — newlib, for
instance, has neither dlopen nor libdl nor dlfcn.h.

libdl is now looked for but not required, and -DHAVE_DLOPEN is defined
when dlopen is available from either place, following the naming the
functions_to_detect loop above already uses. Behaviour is unchanged
where a loader exists: dlopen in libc gives HAVE_DLOPEN and a null
dep_dl exactly as before, dlopen in libdl gives the same -ldl link as
before and now also the define. Only the third case changes, from a
configure error into a build without dlopen.

The formulation is deliberately about the C library rather than about
any particular OS: whether dlopen exists is a libc trait, and platforms
without one keep appearing.

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 3 item 3 (newlib/libnx gaps)
Why: Mesa assumed dlopen is either in libc or in libdl. On
  newlib/libnx (devkitA64, Nintendo Switch) it is in neither: there is
  no dynamic loader, so nothing can be dlopen()ed at all.
Evidence: configuring mesa-26.1.5 for aarch64/horizon with no drivers
  (scripts/configure-mesa.sh) stops at
    Checking for function "dlopen" : NO
    mesa/meson.build:1684:16: ERROR: C shared or static library 'dl' not found
  The same configure reports: Check usable header "dlfcn.h" : NO.
Upstream: yes — it removes an assumption that is not universal and
  changes nothing on any platform that has a loader.
---
 meson.build | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 1eca91f..4cfbd6b 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -1679,9 +1679,19 @@ ld_args_build_id = cc.get_supported_link_arguments('-Wl,--build-id=sha1')
 
 # check for dl support
 dep_dl = null_dep
+with_dlopen = false
 if host_machine.system() != 'windows'
-  if not cc.has_function('dlopen')
-    dep_dl = cc.find_library('dl', required : true)
+  with_dlopen = cc.has_function('dlopen')
+  if not with_dlopen
+    # Older glibc and a few other systems keep dlopen in a separate
+    # libdl. A C library with no dynamic loader at all has neither, and
+    # that is not an error: util/u_dl.c already falls back to reporting
+    # that nothing can be loaded.
+    dep_dl = cc.find_library('dl', required : false)
+    with_dlopen = dep_dl.found()
+  endif
+  if with_dlopen
+    pre_args += '-DHAVE_DLOPEN'
   endif
   if cc.has_function('dladdr', dependencies : dep_dl)
     # This is required for src/util
-- 
